<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>The Lord “sought a man according to His heart,”</l><l>David, as Jesse’s eighth son.</l><l>Even though “he was but a youth,”</l><l>He was God’s anointed one.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>When David found himself in deep distress,</l><l>To Jehovah he would cry:</l><l>“O Jehovah, Thou art my refuge,</l><l>And my source of endless supply!”</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>As David fought “the battles of Jehovah,”</l><l>God was his strength and shield,</l><l>And the rock of his salvation;</l><l>He called, “O Lord!” the vict’ry to wield!</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>The Lord appointed David as ruler,</l><l>Over God’s people as king.</l><l>He would serve according to God’s counsel,</l><l>Writing psalms that now we can sing.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
